    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jackson Merrill** (72.41) serving as our primary engines for offensive production. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** draws a favorable matchup against Burrows, where an elevated SP xERA of 4.71, combined with a strong platoon edge and a prime #2 lineup spot, vaults him into elite territory. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** benefits from the same soft pitching matchup and, crucially, his high stolen base potential\u2014boosted by the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery\u2014makes him a cornerstone play for our category-scarcity strategy. **Kyle Tucker** remains a reliable anchor in our lineup (67.05); despite facing a left-handed pitcher, his inherent power and RBI profile in the #5 spot maintain his high efficiency score against Freeland.\n\nOur decision-making process for the remaining slots remains heavily focused on the Burrows matchup, as **Curtis Mead** (62.15) and **Andy Pages** (62.29) both offer strong, consistent value. **Curtis Mead** narrowly edge out other bench options because the combination of his platoon advantage and batting order stability provided a higher floor than our peripheral depth. Among those who missed the cut, **Drake Baldwin** and **Dominic Smith** are our most precarious starts; both carry a 59.20 and 53.44 score respectively, but they are tethered to the Peralta matchup where a 34% rain risk could jeopardize their full-game participation. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.79) and **Nasim Nunez** (58.62) are projected for respectable performances, **Nasim Nunez** remains a low-priority play due to his #9 lineup position, serving primarily as a defensive fill-in rather than an offensive driver.\n\nManagement remains vigilant regarding our injury report, as **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jorge Polanco** continue to occupy IL spots, limiting our rotation flexibility. With **Gunnar Henderson** off the board due to a team off-day, we are relying on our depth\u2014including the likes of **Josh Lowe**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Sam Antonacci**\u2014to remain ready should the weather risks in the **Drake Baldwin** and **Dominic Smith** game manifest into delays. We are leaning into our current starting nine to exploit the favorable xERA metrics today, prioritizing the speed-oriented upside of **Jackson Merrill** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** to keep our pace in the 5x5 standings.",
